{
  "page_id": "BR-22",
  "section_header": "BRAKE SYSTEM — Rear Brake",
  "title": "REMOVAL OF CYLINDER / DISASSEMBLY OF CYLINDER",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "REMOVAL OF CYLINDER"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(See page BR-20)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "main": "DISCONNECT BRAKE HOSE FROM BRAKE TUBE AND CYLINDER",
          "sub_items": [
            "(a) Using SST and a spanner, disconnect the brake tube from the hose.",
            "SST 09751-36011",
            "(b) Use a container to catch the brake fluid.",
            "(c) Remove the clip from brake hose.",
            "(d) Disconnect the brake hose from the cylinder."
          ]
        },
        {
          "main": "REMOVE CYLINDER",
          "sub_items": [
            "(a) Hold the sliding bushing and unscrew the cylinder installation bolt.",
            "(b) Lift up and push out the cylinder from the torque plate pin."
          ]
        },
        {
          "main": "REMOVE FOLLOWING PARTS:",
          "sub_items": [
            "(a) Anti-squeal shim",
            "(b) Brake pads",
            "(c) Anti-rattle springs",
            "(d) Pad guide plates",
            "(e) Pad support plate"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
